cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use verbatim-citation-gate in research or software, please cite it as below."
title: "verbatim-citation-gate: a two-stage auditor for quote-style RAG citations"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dziatkovskii
    given-names: Anton
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7408-3054"
    affiliation: "Palo Alto AI Research Lab"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Palo-Alto-AI-Research-Lab/verbatim-citation-gate"
url: "https://palo-alto-ai-research-lab.github.io/verbatim-citation-gate/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - citation verification
  - hallucination detection
  - faithfulness
  - LLM evaluation
abstract: >-
  A framework-agnostic auditor for quote-style citations in RAG systems. Stage one
  is a deterministic verbatim gate with no dependencies and no model calls: it
  rejects fabricated quotes, frankenquotes (contiguity, not bag-of-words) and
  surfaces misattributed quotes as a distinct verdict rather than collapsing them
  into "not found". Stage two is a skeptical judge with a burden-of-proof prompt —
  default-refute, outside knowledge inadmissible, support capped at partial unless
  population, direction, magnitude and certainty all match — which fails closed on
  unparseable output. Any LLM plugs in through a two-argument callable.
